course: dictionary
lesson: 10952
title: One word, many jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can change its form and its job. The word wake can be wake, wakes, woke, woken or waking. Context tells you which meaning is in use. «Behind one drawn blind they see a little bird who wakes, yawns and tucks his head back in.» The bird stops sleeping, so wakes means stops sleeping.
explain: Wake can also mean to make someone else stop sleeping. «A boy in Texas woke his hamster in the daytime by poking it.» The boy did not sleep the hamster; he made it stop sleeping. Ask yourself who is doing the waking and who is being woken.
explain: Look for the clue words. «He woke with a start» tells you the person stopped sleeping suddenly. A wake, as a noun, is the line of waves a boat leaves behind it. It is rare, so it is more likely that you will meet wake as a verb in a story.
fact: Wake means to stop sleeping, or to make someone stop sleeping.
fact: The forms are wake, wakes, woke, woken and waking.
fact: «In the wake of» means after something and because of it.
fact: The wake of a boat is the line of waves it leaves behind on the water.
fact: A good check is to swap in another meaning, such as stop sleeping, and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The little bird wakes, yawns and tucks his head back in.» What does wakes mean here? | Builds a new nest | Flies away for ever | *Stops sleeping | Sings a loud song
exercise: «A boy woke his hamster by poking it.» What did the boy do? | Put the hamster to bed | Gave the hamster a bath | Fed the hamster a big meal | *Made the hamster stop sleeping
exercise: The boat left a long wake behind it on the lake. What is the wake? | A tall sail on the mast | *The line of waves left behind on the water | A loud horn that warns other boats | The name painted on the side
test: «Yesterday I woke at seven.» Which word is the past form of wake here? | *woke | wake | waking | wakes
test: «In the wake of the storm, the village was very quiet.» What does in the wake of mean? | Before the storm started | Far away from the storm | During a long sleep | *After the storm, and because of it
exam: «Anna was so quiet that she did not wake the baby.» What does wake mean here? | Hold the baby up high | Give the baby a warm drink | Sing to the baby | *Make the baby stop sleeping
